/-
AtFullSide/K14/RawKeyDefs.lean: A LIST OF KEYS FOR THE NAMES OF THE RAW BOOK's 13,116 ENTRIES
(rawKeysW), MADE OF THE ENTRIES' OWN ADDRESSES AND ONE WRITTEN LIST OF SMALL NUMBERS (rawTagsW); THE
TWO TABLES OF STRINGS PASS tablesOk (rawTables_ok). A WORKING FILE THAT STAYS WITH ITS AUTHORS: IT
SPELLS 5,130 TAGS THAT HANG ON THE ORDER IN WHICH THE FRAME's segmentCarries LAYS ITS ENTRIES.
Definitions; one statement with its proof.

  ownersW, usesW  the four owners' strings and the five uses of Honest/ForKinds.lean
  rawTagsW        for each entry of rawAheadW, in its order, what its fields do not hold of its
                  name: below 64: a spent run: 8 × the number of the owner's string in ownersW + the
                  number of the use in usesW; from 64 on: a carried run: 64 + the message's number.
                  In parts of 256
  keyOf e t       the key (NameKey, Honest/BookLinear/NameKeys.lean): a spent run: the two numbers
                  and e.spender; a carried one: e.owner, the message's number, e.spender
  rawKeysW        List.zipWith keyOf rawAheadW rawTagsW
  rawTables_ok    tablesOk ownersW usesW = true

Why so. A spent entry's name is runName of a string, the entry's spender and a use; a carried one's
carriedName of the entry's owner, a message's number and the entry's spender (the frame's makers:
Want.entry, foldEntries, splitEntry, SentMsg.carry, the own fresh table's carry): both addresses are
the entry's own fields.

WHERE THE TAGS COME FROM: written by a program off a print of Lean's evaluator, which is trusted for
nothing: THAT THEY ARE RIGHT IS rawNames_keys (AtFullSide/K14/RawNamesKeys.lean), by Lean's kernel.
That rawTagsW has 13,116 members is said by no statement here: a list too short would make rawKeysW
too short, and rawNames_keys would fail.

Limits. A FACT ON WRITTEN VALUES: at the proof file's IOP as written in Lean at the full size
(P2Law.ProofPlan.WP), the written sendings (Johnson.G.proofSendsFull) and the merges that
mergesByName lays ("a guess", in the frame's own word): rawAheadW
(AtFullSide/K14/RawAheadWritten.lean) is made at these. rawSegW STANDS OVER THE FRAME's
segmentCarries AS IT IS TODAY. Nothing here says that a key is an entry's. Nothing on any property.
-/
